+# Independent finite partition B derivations
+
+Author SID01a1d840-f94e-7631-aef9-15c312b1ae20. Policy is accepted PLAN43d0e7c8, root adoption and ROOT-POLICY-R6. Exact106case membership/order and baseline identities are completion/PARTITIONS.json. DERIVATIONS.json binds each case's complete raw-line projection, original input digest, rate references, finite expected scope literals, and excluded/nonattempt/unreadable inventory. Input digests include launch/lifecycle/reference-time state and final-newline metadata. No input/history bytes are rewritten. The financial values below were selected from raw usage and policy before reference wiring; the authoring helper serializes a closed literal inventory and imports no canonical financial decisions.
+
+Pinned rate arithmetic, USD per million converted to nano by multiplying token-rate products by1000:
+
+| Raw pricing fact | Independently supported low |
+|---|---|
+| Astra1000 input,100 output, explicit cached/write0 | (1000*10+100*50)*1000=15000000 |
+| Sonnet10000 input, output/cache0 | 10000*2*1000=20000000; Fable alternative high80000000 |
+| Fable1000 input,1000 cache-creation, reported5m1000 | (1000*8+1000*10)*1000=18000000 |
+| Same cache counts with inconsistent extra1h500 | Retain supported18000000; never add the contradictory1500 write split |
+| Astra1000 input,100 output, cached/write null | Minimum all1000 input cached at1, no writes: (1000*1+100*50)*1000=6000000 |
+| Terra12000 output alternative to Astra | 12000*5*1000=60000000; Astra alternative600000000 |
+| Astra12000 output only | 12000*50*1000=600000000 |
+| Astra20000 output, non200 terminal | 20000*50*1000=1000000000 supported usage, despite no complete release |
+| Fable1000 unsplit cache creation | min5m10/1h16 gives10000000; upper16000000 |
+| Fable1000 input,500 output | (1000*8+500*40)*1000=28000000 |
+
+The raw axis assertions and actual Python arithmetic entry points separately check these rates, incomplete bounds, identity sets and local lows. C/F rejection, undercharge, null/string status and conflicts cannot zero already supported usage. The complete priced V01 multiidentity positive remains finite20–80M; undercharge Terra/Astra remains local60M and held800M. Unknown tier7, missing/unrecognized tier, provider/schema mismatch and unpriced identity support no positive minimum. All-null usage observations support0. Reservations, error rows and zero anchors without usage support0. No proxy charge/reservation is repurposed as usage low.
+
+T membership is independently fixed by unique launched session admission. Cases13/105 retain predecessor p ownership; successor s has no seed. No admission, several admitting objectives and unrelated sessions create no owned seed. Window/clock changes do not transfer admitted ownership. None-obligation auxiliary units count in owned_closed under the existing rollup bucket definition; this does not turn their AtLeast0 exposure into a resolved bill. Unowned candidate usage remains in alternative_origin_refs while seed_origin_refs remains empty, including Q8's containing window; Q8's later window has no candidate alternative. Codex exposure is excluded from PiApi owned low. Empty scopes, no-attempt input and unreadable/excluded input have explicit0 assertions and preserved inventory.
+
+R uses single_ambiguous only: no physical independence frame exists. DUP and VC11's two15M observations therefore support15M, never30M. Raw source positions, rid, n and response_id provide no bill-independence grant. All chosen seed and alternative memberships appear in each of224 low assertions and the supplied result. Independent membership is checked against actual wire ownership, so a matching scalar alone cannot satisfy the claim.
+
+VC07 retains its genuine unbudgeted complete15M request plus separate unlinked AtLeast0 auxiliary anchor. Its unchanged raw input has no exact-row link; neither candidate ownership nor the request completion erases that anchor. Its owned scopes remain0 without an admission. Separate earlier conditional link controls remain separate and unchanged.
+
+The supplied computed records are a distinct lane: input proof inventories financial origins and restates only root-approved conditional initial ticket scope (plus inherited C3 exact-byte copy equivalence); result documents carry C witnesses, complete valuation records, inactive hold parents and accepted whole-unit F coverage for the finite Exact positives. Genuine unbudgeted completion has a separate applicability/completion route; Codex has no fabricated F. Per-case provenance payloads name exact conditional scope extents and explicitly leave auxiliary co-reference and physical independence unestablished. Expected assertions supply no grant or F release authority.
+
+Continuity is unestablished because predecessor accounting documents are not supplied in these bundles. Baseline case hashes and preserved inputs/history remain attributable; an opaque hash is not continuity proof. These assertions establish finite supplied corpus checks only, with no arbitrary reducer, executable discovery confluence, live grant, production adapter, integration or S1 acceptance claim.
